  "title": "# Build: banner-widgets (Opus, medium-high thinking; NO Fable on this account) **Name:** Banner wid…",
  "asked": "# Build: banner-widgets (Opus, medium-high thinking; NO Fable on this account) **Name:** Banner widgets · **Category:** Feature ## What Brett said (verbatim, Nov 4 2026, voice) \"I need that [usage meter] to be in the banner too. And then I need to right-click the banner and select which widgets appear in it. It's getting cluttered. And some of them are way too big. I need settings for them all so I can change how big they are, how much room they take up.\" Context: the console banner/top bar holds lots of chips/widgets (Claude badge, Profile, Following Amber, clock, new-changes ticker, % building, axHub status, main build status, Plan, alerts bell, approvals, What's new, No wait, helper widget from Handoff 2 (#338), and soon the Usage meter chip). Existing pieces to REUSE, not duplicate: Settings > Banners (every banner's look/behaviour), banner-pack #251 / banner-editor #254 / banners-one if merged (check), Molly's banner strip (#294), Handoff 2's 'Add widgets' (#338). No new shared contract (no Fable). If a schema change is truly required, use an optional field on the existing banner/chip records and note it for a later Fable review. Book to a free named agent. Plan Studio plan for it. ## Do 1. **Right-click (long-press on phone) the banner > 'Widgets...'** opens a picker listing every available banner widget with a checkbox (show/hide), drag to reorder, and a live preview of the banner. Also from Settings > Banners and the View menu. 2. **Per-widget settings** (right-click any widget > 'Widget settings', and in the picker): **size** (icon only / compact / normal / wide), max width in px or characters with ellipsis, text vs icon vs both, show a number badge only, hide when nothing to report (e.g. 0 alerts), collapse into an overflow '⋯' menu when space runs out, and which region (left / centre / right). Sensible compact defaults so it's not cluttered out of the box; fix the widgets that are too big today (the long ticker text like '130 new · Retire Patches and Build Pilot (remove everywhe...' should be compact by default). 3. **Overflow**: when the bar runs out of room, lowest-priority widgets move into a '⋯' menu automatically (priority set in the picker). 4. Saved per app per device, synced through axHub sync; Reset to default. Works in the console, inside Molly's banner strip, and on phone widths. 5. **Usage meter**: make sure the usage-meter plugin's chip (build `usage-meter`, may land before or after this) registers as a banner widget and appears by default (compact). 6. Every plugin's banner chip registers through one widget registry so new widgets automatically show up in the picker. Add a CI check against hard-coded banner chips. 7. API/MCP/CLI + voice ('hide the clock from the banner', 'make the ticker compact'). AXF tokens only. Basic docs/README.md, tests, phone + desktop UI Review shots (non-blocking). PR **through the merge queue only**. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. ## ADDENDUM 1 (Brett, voice, Nov 4): fast-track \"Start that as a second build right now. Merge it right away. Deploy it.\" - Keep scope tight so it lands tonight: steps 1-5 first, push, open the PR. Steps 6-7 extras only if quick. - The moment CI is green, put the PR at the FRONT of the merge queue (`merge-queue` priority / first in line). Once it's merged, redeploy the console: `cd /opt/axf && git pull --ff-only` then `sudo bash deploy/install-console.sh` (if the deploy fails on a name conflict, `docker rm -f axf-console` first). Confirm https://console.amberxai.com answers 200, then post in the Breakroom chat that it's live. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22…",
